card.statement:
Assume $\MM$ is an irreducible $\LL$-module isomorphic to $\VV_{{\KK}, \vartheta,a}$. For $\KK \subseteq \mathbb N$, set $y_{k,j} = x_{-k,j}$ if $k \in \mathbb N\setminus \KK$ for all $j \in[\mathsf{d}_k]$, and let $y_{k,j} = x_{k,j}$ or $x_{-k,j}$ if $k \in \KK$ for all $j \in[\mathsf{d}_k]$. Then for any nonzero vector $v \in \MM$, the vectors

\begin{equation}   \cdots y_{2,\mathsf{d}_2}^{p_{2,\mathsf{d}_2}} \cdots y_{2,1}^{p_{2,1}} y_{1,\mathsf{d}_1}^{p_{1,\mathsf{d}_1}} \cdots y_{1,1}^{p_{1,1}}v \end{equation}

with exponents $p_{k,j} \in \mathbb N \cup \{0\}$ for all $k,j$ and only finitely many of them nonzero form a basis for $\MM$.
